marks#1-what-is-measured","content":"**Answer quality:** task-specific judge score or accuracy.","locale":"en"},"555":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-27","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#1-what-is-measured","content":"**Input tokens:** model context consumed while the agent works.","locale":"en"},"556":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-28","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#1-what-is-measured","content":"**Tool calls:** search and inspection actions recorded in the trajectory.","locale":"en"},"557":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-29","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#1-what-is-measured","content":"**Agent wall time:** task execution time, excluding Zvec-Grep index preparation.","locale":"en"},"558":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-30","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#1-what-is-measured","content":"Quality should stay stable or improve. Tokens, tool calls, and wall time should decrease.","locale":"en"},"559":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-31","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#swe-qa-bench","content":"Measures repository-level, cross-file, and multi-hop software-engineering question answering. It is designed for questions where the relevant implementation is distributed across a codebase and the entry point is not known in advance.","locale":"en"},"560":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-32","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#swe-qa-bench","content":"Read the SWE-QA-Bench setup and methodology","locale":"en"},"561":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-33","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#browsecomp-plus","content":"Measures multi-document evidence retrieval and answer accuracy over a large, fixed text corpus. It tests whether ranked semantic and lexical evidence reduces broad document scanning without lowering answer quality.","locale":"en"},"562":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-34","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#browsecomp-plus","content":"Read the BrowseComp-Plus setup and methodology","locale":"en"},"563":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-35","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#3-how-to-interpret-the-results","content":"The results show the effect of adding Zvec-Grep to an agent workflow; they are not a raw CLI latency comparison. Agent behavior is stochastic, so repeated-run averages are more useful than a single trial.","locale":"en"},"564":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-36","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#3-how-to-interpret-the-results","content":"The largest efficiency gains appear when a task requires semantic discovery, cross-file synthesis, or evidence spread across many documents. For a known literal or symbol, native ripgrep may still be the most direct route.","locale":"en"},"565":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-37","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#4-reproduce-the-evaluation","content":"Both suites pin their inputs and dependencies, keep generated artifacts outside the agent-visible workspace, and provide their own runner and reporting workflow.","locale":"en"},"566":{"id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks-38","page_id":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/zvec-grep/benchmarks#4-reproduce-the-evaluation","content":"Open the complete benchmark documentation","locale":"en"},"567":{"id":"/en/doc