sert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A scalar field: `text` (string)","locale":"en"},"1547":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A dense vector embedding: `text_embedding` (4-dimensional FP32 vector)","locale":"en"},"1548":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The 4-dimensional vector is for demonstration only — real-world embeddings are usually much larger.","locale":"en"},"1549":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"You've also opened the collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1550":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Now, insert a document like this:","locale":"en"},"1551":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The `insert()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1552":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1553":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the insertion and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., duplicate `ID`, insufficient disk space).","locale":"en"},"1554":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Successfully inserted documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1555":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To insert multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `insert()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1556":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are inserted**.","locale":"en"},"1557":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to insert every one. A failure in one (e.g., duplicate `id`) does **not** stop others from being inserted.","locale":"en"},"1558":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1559":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Assume your collection includes a sparse vector named `sparse_embedding`.","locale":"en"},"1560":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert a document with a sparse vector like this:","locale":"en"},"1561":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"A sparse vector is represented as a mapping from `dimension indices` (integers) to `values` (floats).\\\nThere is **no fixed dimension size** — only non-zero dimensions need to be included.","locale":"en"},"1562":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Real-world applications often require collections with multiple scalar fields and vector embeddings. In this example, assume your collection includes the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1563":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1564":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1565":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1566":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1567":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1568":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1569":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1570":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert a document with multiple fields and vectors like this:","locale":"en"},"1571":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"page","content":"Iterate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","locale":"en"},"1572":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"Select Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1573":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Snapshot Semantics","locale":"en"},"1574":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Concurrency","locale":"en"},"1575":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Break Early","locale":"en"},"1576":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Use &#x2A;*`iter_docs()`** to stream **all** documents in a collection one by one.","locale":"en"},"1577":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Unlike `fetch()` — which retrieves documents by known `id`s — iteration performs a **full scan**. Documents are streamed in bounded windows, so the whole collection is never materialized in memory at once — making it suitable for export, backup, migration, or offline processing.","locale":"en"},"1578":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"The iterator holds a native resource slot on the collection, so let the language close it for you: Python's `with` statement and JavaScript's `for...of` loop both release the iterator when the loop finishes, breaks early, or raises an exception. Iterators also close themselves automatically when fully exhausted.","locale":"en"},"1579":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"By default, every scalar field and every vector is materialized for each document. Use `output_fields` and `include_vector` to reduce the amount of data read:","locale":"en"},"1580":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`output_fields`** (`outputFields`): a list of scalar field names to return. If omitted, all scalar fields are returned; an empty list returns no scalar fields. Unknown or duplicate names raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1581":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`include_vector`** (`includeVector`): whether to materialize vector data. Vectors are included by default; disable it when you only need scalar fields — skipping vectors makes traversal faster.","locale":"en"},"1582":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Both `iter_docs()` and `iterDocsSync()` iterate over an **isolated snapshot taken at call time**:","locale":"en"},"1583":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Data written **after** the iterator is created — inserts, upserts, updates — is **not visible** to this iterator.","locale":"en"},"1584":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Deletes made after creation do not affect the iteration; documents already deleted when the snapshot was taken are filtered out.","locale":"en"},"1585":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"On a writable collection, creating the iterator may seal the current writing segment (each call can produce a new small segment); read-only collections are scanned directly without any write.","locale":"en"},"1586":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Iteration order is unspecified — it is **not** insertion order, and it can change after `optimize()` reorganizes segments — so never rely on it.","locale":"en"},"1587":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"While any iterator is open on a collection, these operations **raise an error**:","locale":"en"},"1588":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Schema changes — creating or dropping an index, adding, altering or dropping a column","locale":"en"},"1589":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"`optimize()`, which fails at its start","locale":"en"},"1590":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Closing or destroying the collection","locale":"en"},"1591":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Conversely, creating an iterator fails while one of those maintenance operations is already running. Writes, `flush()`, `query()` and `fetch()` remain **unaffected**.","locale":"en"},"1592":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Close every iterator before closing the collection. These restrictions are lifted as soon as all open iterators are closed.","locale":"en"},"1593":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Stopping before the end is safe — exiting the `with` block or the `for...of` loop releases the iterator's slot. When you drive the iterator manually instead, close it yourself:","locale":"en"},"1594":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"page","content":"Update","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","locale":"en"},"1595":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1596":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Update a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1597":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Update a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1598":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Use `update()` to modify **existing** documents (`Doc`).","locale":"en"},"1599":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Only the scalar fields and vector embeddings you **include will be updated**; all other content remains unchanged.","locale":"en"},"1600":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"The method accepts either a single `Doc` object or a list of `Doc` objects.","locale":"en"},"1601":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `update()` must:","locale":"en"},"1602":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Specify an `id` that **already exists** in the collection (the operation will fail if the document is not found)","locale":"en"},"1603":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Include only the fields and vectors you **intend to update**, formatted according to the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1604":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1605":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1606":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Omit any scalar fields or vectors you do not want to change — they will be left untouched.","locale":"en"},"1607":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1608":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1609":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1610":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1611":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1612":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1613":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1614":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1615":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"To update an existing document, provide its `id` and only the fields or vectors you want to change:","locale":"en"},"1616":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"The `update()` method validates the document first:","locale":"en"},"1617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**Incorrect usage** — such as an unknown field or wrong vector dimension — **raises an error**.","locale":"en"},"1618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"**If validation passes**, the method proceeds with the update and returns a `Status` object indicating success or failure (e.g., non-existing `ID`).","locale":"en"},"1619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Successfully updated documents are immediately available for querying 🚀.","locale":"en"},"1620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"To update multiple documents at once, pass a list of `Doc` objects to `update()`.\\\nEach `Doc` is processed independently, and the method returns a list of `Status` objects — one per document.","locale":"en"},"1621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are updated**.","locale":"en"},"1622":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to update every one. A failure in one (e.g., the `id` doesn't exist) does **not** stop others from being updated.","locale":"en"},"1623":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1624":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"page","content":"Upsert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","locale":"en"},"1625":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1626":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-single-document","content":"Upsert a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1627":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Upsert a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1628":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Upsert Documents with Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1629":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#upsert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Upsert Documents with Multiple Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1630":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"`upsert()` works similar to `insert()` — it adds one or more new documents (`Doc`) to a collection.","locale":"en"},"1631":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"The key difference is that if a document with the same `id` already exists, it will be **overwritten**.","locale":"en"},"1632":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"Use `upsert()` if you want to overwrite an existing document (or don't mind replacing it).","locale":"en"},"1633":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"Use `insert()` if you want to avoid accidentally overwriting a document — `insert()` will fail if a document with the same id already exists.","locale":"en"},"1634":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","content":"**Performance Tip**:\\\nNew vectors are initially buffered for fast ingestion. For optimal search performance, call `optimize()` after upserting a large batch of documents.","locale":"en"},"1635":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `upsert()` must:","locale":"en"},"1636":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Have an `id` (if a document with the same `id` already exists, it will be replaced)","locale":"en"},"1637":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert#document-doc","content":"Provide data that matches the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1638":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/upsert","tags":[],