ity scores depends on the metric used by the vector field. For example, higher inner product scores usually indicate greater relevance, while lower L2 and cosine distance scores usually indicate greater relevance.","locale":"en"},"2539":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-116","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#results","content":"The grouping field value is returned independently of the output fields. You can use it to identify a group even when the grouping field is not included in the output fields.","locale":"en"},"2540":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-117","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Grouped search supports only single-vector search. It does not support full-text search or multi-vector search.","locale":"en"},"2541":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-118","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"The grouping field cannot be a vector or array field.","locale":"en"},"2542":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-119","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Grouped search currently does not support IVF, DiskANN, or Vamana vector indexes.","locale":"en"},"2543":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-120","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Grouped search cannot be used with vector refinement (refiner).","locale":"en"},"2544":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-121","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Grouped search is best-effort. Depending on the data distribution and search conditions, the actual number of groups and documents per group may be lower than the specified values. When there are not enough candidates, Zvec prioritizes the number of groups.","locale":"en"},"2545":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group-122","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/group#limitations-and-considerations","content":"Increasing the number of groups or documents per group requires collecting and sorting more candidates and typically increases query latency.","locale":"en"},"2546":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","type":"page","content":"Vector + Filter","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","locale":"en"},"2547":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2548":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#performing-filtered-vector-search","content":"Performing Filtered Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2549":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","content":"You can combine **vector search** with **scalar filters** to restrict results to a subset of documents — just like adding a `WHERE` clause to a similarity search.","locale":"en"},"2550":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes you:","locale":"en"},"2551":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#prerequisites","content":"Have already opened a `collection` instance.","locale":"en"},"2552":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#prerequisites","content":"Are familiar with vector querying and conditional filtering.","locale":"en"},"2553":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains one dense vector field `dense_embedding` and one scalar field `publish_year`.","locale":"en"},"2554":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#performing-filtered-vector-search","content":"To combine vector similarity search with filters, pass both a query specification and a `filter` expression to the `query()` method.","locale":"en"},"2555":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/hybrid#performing-filtered-vector-search","content":"This returns the top-10 most similar documents that satisfy `publish_year > 1936`, sorted by similarity score.","locale":"en"},"2556":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"page","content":"Query","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","locale":"en"},"2557":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"`Query`","locale":"en"},"2558":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"Query Types","locale":"en"},"2559":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#quick-start-examples","content":"Quick Start Examples","locale":"en"},"2560":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#single-vector-search","content":"Single-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2561":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#multi-vector-search","content":"Multi-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2562":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#conditional-filtering","content":"Conditional Filtering","locale":"en"},"2563":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#hybrid-search","content":"Hybrid Search","locale":"en"},"2564":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#full-text-search","content":"Full-Text Search","locale":"en"},"2565":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#grouped-search","content":"Grouped Search","locale":"en"},"2566":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","content":"The `query()` method supports **vector similarity search**, **full-text search** (BM25 ranking), **conditional filtering** (like a SQL `WHERE` clause), or **combinations of these**.","locale":"en"},"2567":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","content":"It returns a list of `Doc` objects, each containing the matched document and its relevance score.","locale":"en"},"2568":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"In Zvec, a `Query` is a query specification that describes the field and query source used for a search. Query APIs accept one or more `Query` specifications depending on whether you are performing a single- or multi-query search.","locale":"en"},"2569":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"A single `Query` can target either vector search or full-text search, but not both at the same time.","locale":"en"},"2570":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"Each `Query` specifies:","locale":"en"},"2571":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"`field_name`: The name of the vector or full-text field to search","locale":"en"},"2572":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"**Query source**:","locale":"en"},"2573":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"For vector search, provide an explicit `vector` or a document `id` (to reuse the stored embedding of an existing document)","locale":"en"},"2574":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"For full-text search, provide an `fts` clause","locale":"en"},"2575":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"`param` (optional): Index-specific query parameters (e.g., `ef` for HNSW or `default_operator` for full-text search)","locale":"en"},"2576":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"Each `ZVecQuery` specifies:","locale":"en"},"2577":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"`fieldName`: The name of the vector or full-text field to search","locale":"en"},"2578":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"**Query source**:","locale":"en"},"2579":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"For vector search, provide `vector`","locale":"en"},"2580":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"For full-text search, provide `fts`","locale":"en"},"2581":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query","content":"`params` (optional): Index-specific query parameters (e.g., `ef` for HNSW or `defaultOperator` for full-text search)","locale":"en"},"2582":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Single-Vector Search\" description=\"Find documents using a single vector embedding\" href=\"./single-vector/\" icon=\"<Search className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2583":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Multi-Vector Search\" description=\"Combine multiple embeddings with re-ranking\" href=\"./multi-vector/\" icon=\"<Layers className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2584":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Conditional Filtering\" description=\"Filter documents using scalar field conditions\" href=\"./filter/\" icon=\"<Filter className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2585":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Filtered Vector Search\" description=\"Combine vector search with conditional filters\" href=\"./hybrid/\" icon=\"<Combine className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2586":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Full-Text Search\" description=\"Search documents by text content with BM25 ranking\" href=\"./fts/\" icon=\"<Type className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2587":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query#query-types","content":"<Card title=\"Grouped Search\" description=\"Group vector search results by a scalar field\" href=\"./group/\" icon=\"<Rows3 className=&#x22;text-blue-300&#x22; />\" />","locale":"en"},"2588":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"page","content":"Multiple Vectors","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","locale":"en"},"2589":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2590":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Performing Multi-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2591":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranking Strategies","locale":"en"},"2592":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"Zvec supports **multi-vector queries**, allowing you to combine different embeddings in a single search.","locale":"en"},"2593":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"When querying multiple vector embeddings, Zvec retrieves candidates from each vector space independently and then fuses them into one relevance-ordered list. Because scores from different vector spaces might not be directly comparable, you must choose a suitable **re-ranking strategy**.","locale":"en"},"2594":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes:","locale":"en"},"2595":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You have opened a `collection` with multiple vector fields","locale":"en"},"2596":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You're familiar with the basic vector querying concepts. If not, please review the single-vector search guide","locale":"en"},"2597":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2598":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2599":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2600":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2601":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"In Python, pass a list of query specifications to `query()` and provide a fusion strategy through `reranker`. In Node.js, pass the sub-queries to `multiQuerySync()` or `multiQuery()` and configure `rerank`.","locale":"en"},"2602":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"This example queries both `dense_embedding` and `sparse_embedding` and uses `WeightedReRanker` to combine their results. Weights are positional and must follow the same order as `queries`.","locale":"en"},"2603":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topk` always controls the number of **final documents** returned after fusion.","locale":"en"},"2604":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Python does not currently expose a separate candidate-count option for each sub-query in `Collection.query()`.","locale":"en"},"2605":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Node.js supports `numCandidates` on each sub-query. If omitted, its default is `max(topk, 10)`.","locale":"en"},"2606":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topn` is used only when calling a re-ranker's standalone `rerank()` method; it is not a constructor argument.","locale":"en"},"2607":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Zvec provides different re-ranking strategies to combine scores from multiple vector fields.","locale":"en"},"2608":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranker","locale":"en"},"2609":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`WeightedReRanker`","locale":"en"},"2610":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`RrfReRanker` (Reciprocal Rank Fusion)","locale":"en"},"2611":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Approach","locale":"en"},"2612":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Combines normalized similarity scores using **custom weights**","locale":"en"},"2613":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Fuses results based only on **ranking positions** — no scores needed  With a zero-based rank *r* (the first result is 0), the RRF score is: $\\text{RRF}(r) = \\frac{1}{k + r + 1}$","locale":"en"},"2614":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"2615":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores are reasonably comparable across vector fields  • You know the relative importance of each embedding type","locale":"en"},"2616":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores come from different metrics or scales  • You prefer a simple, robust, tuning-free method","locale":"en"},"2617":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2618":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`weights`: An ordered list aligned with `queries`. Score normalization uses each queried field's schema.","locale":"en"},"2619":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`rank_constant` (*k*): Controls how quickly rank influence decreases. Higher values reduce the dominance of top-ranked results.","locale":"en"},"2620":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"page","content":"Single Vector","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","locale":"en"},"2621":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/si